    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **64 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key and duplicate detection to match the specification. Changes:\n\n**`Owner.java`** (model):\n- `getIdentityKey()` now returns the SHA-256 hex over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (previously an unhashed `telephone|email|householdId` string).\n- Added a shared static `identityKey(telephone, email, lastName)` helper plus a standard American **Soundex** implementation (`soundex`/`soundexDigit`) and a `sha256Hex` helper.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n- `rejectDuplicateIdentity` now compares the new SHA-256 identity key against existing non-deleted owners (still ignoring soft-deleted owners; the disposable-email-domain blocklist still runs first in `normalizeEmail`, before this check). Removed the old `identityKeyFor` helper in favor of `Owner.identityKey`.\n- **Removed the separate household-duplicate 409 block** (`rejectDuplicateHousehold` and its call) \u2014 duplicate detection is now the single identity key. Two owners with the same lastName + postcode but different telephones now get created (as a soft match), not rejected.\n- `assignPossibleDuplicate` now soft-matches when **soundex(lastName) and postcode match but the identityKey differs**, flagging the earliest such owner (previously matched on case-insensitive lastName + postcode + different telephone).\n- Removed the now-unused `DuplicateHouseholdException` import and fixed dangling javadoc references.\n\n`householdId` itself is retained (still derived from lastName + postcode, still used for `householdMemberCount` and the membership-level cap) \u2014 only the 409 rejection based on it was removed, per the spec.\n\nBehavior verified across the directly-affected checkpoints (Cp03, Cp10, Cp11, Cp13, Cp23, Cp25, Cp28, Cp35, Cp36, Cp39, Cp52) and the full suite with no regressions.",
